  "raw": {
    "https://longwood.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205325": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of CBE Student Success (FA048)",
      "description": "Longwood University\nJob Posting: Assistant Director of CBE Student Success (FA048) Longwood University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Director of CBE Student Success (FA048) Title Careers Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Director of CBE Student Success (FA048) Category: Administrative/Professional Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: College of Business and Economics Locations: Farmville, VA Posted: Sep 29, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Exempt Ref. No.: FA048 Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $45,000.00 - $50,000.00 Position ID: 205325 Share About Longwood University: A comprehensive university with a strong liberal arts foundation, Longwood has a distinctive mission to develop citizen leaders who are prepared to make positive contributions to the common good of society. Founded in 1839, Longwood is the third-oldest public university in Virginia. Longwood is part of the proud tradition of higher education in the Commonwealth of Virginia. Roughly one hour's drive from Charlottesville, Lynchburg, and Richmond, Longwood is located in the historic two-college community of Farmville.  Longwood currently has approximately 4,700 undergraduate and graduate students and 42,000 alumni. It maintains affiliations with the neighboring Robert Russa Moton Museum of civil rights history and the Longwood Center for Visual Arts, a nationally accredited university art museum. A member of the Big South Conference, Longwood competes at the NCAA Division I level. Job Description: Longwood University seeks applicants for the Assistant Director of CBE Student Success (FA048) in the College of Business and Economics (CBE). The Assistant Director for CBE Student Success will support academic advising, employer engagement, and event operations. This role is responsible for helping students navigate academic and professional pathways, strengthening relationships with employers, and coordinating programs and events that advance student success and career readiness. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: College of Business and Economics Student Advising: Provide academic advising to students regarding degree requirements, major and career exploration, course selection, academic policies, and progress toward graduation. Help develop and implement advising programs, workshops, and student success initiatives. Collaborate with faculty, staff, academic departments, student services, and campus partners to support student retention and graduation. Support data collection, reporting, and assessment efforts related to advising outcomes and student success. Assist with student onboarding programs such as orientation, CBE first-year experience course, and other activities. Manage academic honor society for the college. CBE Student Success and McGaughy Internship and Professional Development Center Events and Administrative Support: Coordinate planning and execution of signature events for CBE Student Success and McGaughy Internship and Professional Development Center. Assist with event and program communications, marketing development and distribution. Verify and submit expense reports and invoices for events and programs Work with potential employers, campus partners, and community members to plan and execute professional development and student success events. Maintain and order inventory for teams This position is located in Farmville, Virginia, and is required to work in person on Longwood University's campus. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in business, communication, or any related field from an accredited institution. Strong interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills are required, along with the ability to work effectively with students, faculty, staff, employers, and external partners. Candidates should demonstrate strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines. Proficiency with standard office technology and ability to learn the Banner system in a short period of time. Preferred Qualifications: Experience advising or supporting undergraduate students in a higher education setting, particularly in academic advising, internships, career services, student success, or employer relations is preferred. Experience planning and coordinating student-focused programs, career events, employer engagement activities, or professional development initiatives. Additional Information: This is a full-time, administrative & professional faculty, exempt position. The anticipated salary range for this position will be $45,000 to $50,000 annually. A successful fingerprint-based criminal background investigation is required. AmeriCorps, Peace Corps, and other national service alumni are encouraged to apply. Commonwealth of Virginia benefits accompany this position to include: State health and dental benefits & flexible spending accounts Paid leave (which may include sick leave, personal leave, annual leave, etc.), and 13 holidays Retirement savings plans (some with limited employer match available (VRS)) Life & Long-Term care insurance Employee Assistance Program Employee discounts for various services, including Verizon Educational benefits for most employees Cost-effective Fitness Center membership for employees In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), Longwood University will provide, if requested, reasonable accommodations to applicants in order to provide access to the application and/or interview process. You are not required to note the presence of a disability on your application. If, however, you require accommodations in the application and/or interview process, please contact the Office of Human Resources at 434-395-2074 or humres@longwood.edu . Per CFR: Title 34, the Title IX Coordinator's contact information can be located through this link http://www.longwood.edu/titleix/ . A diversified workforce is an important part of our strategic plan.  EOE/AA Application Instructions: Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled; position posted 9/29/2026. To apply for this position, qualified applicants must complete the online information section and questions, and attach (under Resume): letter of interest resume names and contact details of three references Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Longwood University 201 High Street Farmville, VA 23909"
    },
    "https://longwood.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204294": {
      "title": "Director of Administrative Operations for the Longwood Center for the Visual Arts (FA149)",
      "description": "Longwood University\nJob Posting: Director of Administrative Operations for the Longwood Center for the Visual Arts (FA149) Longwood University \n\tJob Posting: Director of Administrative Operations for the Longwood Center for the Visual Arts (FA149) Title Careers Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Director of Administrative Operations for the Longwood Center for the Visual Arts (FA149) Category: Administrative/Professional Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Longwood Center for the Visual Arts Locations: Farmville, VA Posted: Aug 31, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Exempt Ref. No.: FA149 Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $62,000.00 - $70,000.00 Position ID: 204294 Share About Longwood University: A comprehensive university with a strong liberal arts foundation, Longwood has a distinctive mission to develop citizen leaders who are prepared to make positive contributions to the common good of society. Founded in 1839, Longwood is the third-oldest public university in Virginia. Longwood is part of the proud tradition of higher education in the Commonwealth of Virginia. Roughly one hour's drive from Charlottesville, Lynchburg, and Richmond, Longwood is located in the historic two-college community of Farmville. Longwood currently has approximately 4,600 undergraduate and graduate students and 41,000 alumni. It maintains affiliations with the neighboring Robert Russa Moton Museum of civil rights history and the Longwood Center for Visual Arts, a nationally accredited university art museum. A member of the Big South Conference, Longwood competes at the NCAA Division I level. Job Description: The Longwood Center for the Visual Arts (LCVA) invites applications for a Director of Administrative Operations (FA149). The LCVA is Longwood University's American Alliance of Museums-accredited art museum, located on the corner of Main and Third Streets in downtown Farmville. Its renowned collection includes outstanding examples of American, African, and Chinese Art. In particular, the museum's American Collection features 19th-, 20th-, and 21st-century works, with an impressive subset of Contemporary Folk Art and art by Virginians. Temporary exhibitions highlight historic and contemporary works of national acclaim. The permanent collection is also exhibited in all academic buildings throughout Longwood's campus, including five named galleries. The LCVA's educational programs span the breadth and depth of art and focus on engaging the public and regional schools on the importance of art in everyday life. The Director of Administrative Operations is responsible for managing museum operations with regard to facilities, budget, and visitor services, ensuring that the standards for accredited museums from the American Alliance of Museums are met, and ensuring that Longwood University and LCVA policies and procedures are followed. This position will also assist the Executive Director with strategic and budget planning, calendar and project management, and donor, advisory board, and stakeholder relations. Facility & Operations Management Fully understand, interpret, and implement Longwood and LCVA policies and procedures, especially with regard to art facility management including but not limited to security, climate control, and safety. Ensure policies and procedures are followed. Master and apply American Alliance of Museums standards and best practices, to ensure LCVA's compliance as an AAM-accredited museum. Recruit, hire, train, schedule, and supervise student workers who serve as gallery attendants. Assist in onboarding new staff when needed. Serve as building coordinator, log, manage, and ensure timely and accurate completion of work orders and ensure facilities are safe, clean, and well-maintained on a daily basis. Provide oversight of the museum's security and environmental controls, implementing safety standards, emergency planning, training, and testing, and ensuring business continuity. Keep logs of access permissions, inventoried University property, and up-to-date emergency contact information and ensure university offices have accurate information. Maintain positive and proactive relationships with Longwood University offices, including facilities, campus police, and IT. Budget & Project Management Serve as the key liaison between the LCVA and Academic Affairs budget and procurement personnel. Assist Executive Director and the staff in developing the annual budget plan, exhibition plan, and programming schedule; track projects to ensure schedule is met. Track financial and donor contributions, budgets, and expenditures to ensure that staff remain within annual budget plans and follow budget policies and procedures. Serve as the Executive Director's proxy in approval of leave time for staff and check leave balances, log approvals, ensure leave is noted on calendars. Manage the Executive Director's calendar and represent the Executive Director's views to various stakeholders in his absence. Visitor, Donor, Advisory Board, and Stakeholder Relations Staff the main phone line and email account of the LCVA, responding to all inquiries in a timely, accurate, and courteous manner. Maintain accurate and current database of donors, advisory board members, and museum supporters. Ensure RaisersEdge is up-to-date. Communicate with and maintain positive relations with donors, advisory board members, and other University and community stakeholders. Draft for Executive Director's approval and manage the production and mailing of annual gift solicitation letters and donor proposals. Plan and execute donor events and LCVA Advisory Board meetings, including but not limited to invitations, scheduling, layouts, hospitality for guests, and itineraries. Prepare for, attend, and write minutes of meetings of the LCVA Advisory Board and ensure committee staff liaisons write minutes and submit for committee meetings. Assist Executive Director with writing and proofreading as needed. This position is located in Farmville, Virginia, and is required to work in person on Longwood University's campus. Some night and weekend work will be required. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Required qualifications: Bachelor's degree (arts or museum studies preferred) from an accredited institution. Excellent interpersonal, communication (oral and written), and customer service skills. A high degree of professionalism is required. Excellent organizational and project management skills, with an eye for detail. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple tasks and projects simultaneously. Ability to work with all types of constituents including University and corporate leaders, donors, faculty, students, administrators, community members, colleagues, schoolteachers, and volunteers. Must work some nights and weekends as needed. Preferred qualifications: Master's degree in the field of arts or museum studies from an accredited institution. Proven success in managing an organizational budget. Experience working in a museum setting and familiarity with AAM accreditation standards. Prior work experience in a university or college setting. Additional Information: This is a full-time, administrative & professional faculty, exempt position. The anticipated salary range for this position will be $62,000 to $70,000 annually. A successful fingerprint-based criminal background investigation is required. AmeriCorps, Peace Corps, and other national service alumni are encouraged to apply. Commonwealth of Virginia benefits accompany this position to include: State health and dental benefits & flexible spending accounts Paid leave (which may include sick leave, personal leave, annual leave, etc.), and 13 holidays Retirement savings plans (some with limited employer match available (VRS)) Life & Long-Term care insurance Employee Assistance Program Employee discounts for various services, including Verizon Educational benefits for most employees Cost-effective Fitness Center membership for employees In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), Longwood University will provide, if requested, reasonable accommodations to applicants in order to provide access to the application and/or interview process. You are not required to note the presence of a disability on your application. If, however, you require accommodations in the application and/or interview process, please contact the Office of Human Resources at 434-395-2074 or humres@longwood.edu . Per CFR: Title 34, the Title IX Coordinator's contact information can be located through this link http://www.longwood.edu/titleix/ . A diversified workforce is an important part of our strategic plan.  EOE/AA Application Instructions: Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled; position posted 8/31/2026. To apply for this position, qualified applicants must complete the online information section and questions, and please attach (under Resume): Letter of interest Resume Names and contact details for three references Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Longwood University 201 High Street Farmville, VA 23909"
    },
    "https://longwood.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204799": {
      "title": "Carpenter / Trades Technician III (00052)",
      "description": "Longwood University\nJob Posting: Carpenter / Trades Technician III (00052) Longwood University \n\tJob Posting: Carpenter / Trades Technician III (00052) Title Careers Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Carpenter / Trades Technician III (00052) Category: Classified Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Facilities Management and Operations Locations: Farmville, VA Posted: Sep 14, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Non-Exempt Ref. No.: (00052) Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $42,000.00 - $47,000.00 Position ID: 204799 Share About Longwood University: A comprehensive university with a strong liberal arts foundation, Longwood has a distinctive mission to develop citizen leaders who are prepared to make positive contributions to the common good of society. Founded in 1839, Longwood is the third-oldest public university in Virginia. Longwood is part of the proud tradition of higher education in the Commonwealth of Virginia. Roughly one hour's drive from Charlottesville, Lynchburg, and Richmond, Longwood is located in the historic two-college community of Farmville. Longwood currently has approximately 4,600 undergraduate and graduate students and 41,000 alumni. It maintains affiliations with the neighboring Robert Russa Moton Museum of civil rights history and the Longwood Center for Visual Arts, a nationally accredited university art museum. A member of the Big South Conference, Longwood competes at the NCAA Division I level. Job Description: Longwood University invites qualified applicants to apply for the position of Carpenter / Trades Technician III (00052). The successful candidate will perform highly skilled carpentry work, including but not limited to repairs, installations, remodeling, and maintenance. This position is considered to be emergency personnel, and must report to work or be called in due to inclement weather, in the case of emergency, staff shortage, etc. This position is located in Farmville, Virginia, and is required to work in person on Longwood University's campus. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Essential Responsibilities and Duties: Perform layout work and assess project requirements Conduct new installations or renovations of buildings on or around campus Order parts and materials, ensuring accurate cost allocation and documentation Perform repair work on campus buildings, both inside and outside, including structural and cosmetic repairs Prioritize and complete tasks within the designated timeframe specified by the requester Conduct daily campus-wide inspections to identify and resolve any necessary repairs Perform in-shop work to repair or construct new items such as cabinets, boxes, bookshelves, etc. Comply with all OSHA safety standards and regulations Complete work orders with accurate labor and material costs Maintain a neat and orderly shop and truck inventory, ensuring that unused items are returned to their proper locations Adhere to all local and state codes Occasionally review labor and material bids for carpentry jobs Requirements: High school diploma or equivalent Valid Virginia driver's license Journeyman-level experience in commercial or residential carpentry Proven ability to effectively use a diverse range of tools and machinery Extensive knowledge in repairing door hardware and all panic devices Basic knowledge of computer and work order systems Additional Information: This is a full-time, classified, non-exempt position in pay band 3. The anticipated salary range for this position is $42,000 - $47,000 annually. A successful fingerprint-based criminal background investigation is required. AmeriCorps, Peace Corps, and other national service alumni are encouraged to apply. Commonwealth of Virginia benefits accompany this position to include: State health and dental benefits & flexible spending accounts Paid leave (which may include sick leave, personal leave, annual leave, etc.), and 13 holidays Retirement savings plans (some with limited employer match available (VRS)) Life & Long-Term care insurance Employee Assistance Program Employee discounts for various services, including Verizon Educational benefits for most employees Cost-effective Fitness Center membership for employees In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), Longwood University will provide, if requested, reasonable accommodations to applicants in order to provide access to the application and/or interview process. You are not required to note the presence of a disability on your application. If, however, you require accommodations in the application and/or interview process, please contact the Office of Human Resources at 434-395-2074 or humres@longwood.edu . Per CFR: Title 34, the Title IX Coordinator's contact information can be located through this link http://www.longwood.edu/titleix/ . A diversified workforce is an important part of our strategic plan. EOE/AA Application Instructions: Review of applications will begin immediately. Position will be posted a minimum of five business days. Position posted 9/14/2026. To apply for this position, qualified applicants must complete the online application and attach a resume and cover letter, and any other documents you wish to include. If you have been affected by DHRM Policy 1.30 Layoff, and possess a valid Interagency Placement Screening Form (Yellow Card) or a Preferential Hiring Card (Blue Card), you must upload a copy of your card when you submit your application/resume. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Longwood University 201 High Street Farmville, VA 23909"
    },
    "https://longwood.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=198646": {
      "title": "Police Officer / Law Enforcement Officer I (00224)",
      "description": "Longwood University\nJob Posting: Police Officer / Law Enforcement Officer I (00224) Longwood University \n\tJob Posting: Police Officer / Law Enforcement Officer I (00224) Title Careers Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Police Officer / Law Enforcement Officer I (00224) Category: Classified Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Police & Public Safety Locations: Farmville, VA Posted: Mar 27, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Non-Exempt Ref. No.: (00224) Position ID: 198646 Share About Longwood University: A comprehensive university with a strong liberal arts foundation, Longwood has a distinctive mission to develop citizen leaders who are prepared to make positive contributions to the common good of society. Founded in 1839, Longwood is the third-oldest public university in Virginia. Longwood is part of the proud tradition of higher education in the Commonwealth of Virginia. Roughly one hour's drive from Charlottesville, Lynchburg, and Richmond, Longwood is located in the historic two-college community of Farmville.  Longwood currently has approximately 4,600 undergraduate and graduate students and 41,000 alumni. It maintains affiliations with the neighboring Robert Russa Moton Museum of civil rights history and the Longwood Center for Visual Arts, a nationally accredited university art museum. A member of the Big South Conference, Longwood competes at the NCAA Division I level. Job Description: Longwood University invites qualified applicants to apply for the position of Police Officer / Law Enforcement Officer I (00224) in the Department of Police and Public Safety. Successful candidates will provide professional police service to the Longwood University community and the Town of Farmville. Police Officers are an essential part of Longwood University's diverse and vibrant community as they ensure a secure environment for one of the Commonwealth's Division I universities. As a 24/7 law enforcement agency, staff may be assigned to work multiple shifts, including nights, weekends, and holidays, to meet operational needs. This position is considered emergency personnel. Staff must report to work or be called in during inclement weather, emergencies, or staff shortages. Selected candidates are expected to work 12-hour shifts, day or night, based on department needs. Overtime work outside normal shift hours may be required. This position is located in Farmville, Virginia, and is required to work in person on Longwood University's campus. Essential Responsibilities and Duties: Provide professional police services to the University community and the community at large while conducting patrols and responding to calls for service within the Longwood University police jurisdictional area Investigate complaints, suspicious activity, and crime/traffic accidents Execute arrests, prepare and issue citations, preserve and document evidence, and deliver legal papers Ensure the safety and security of individuals and property by upholding laws and responding effectively to emergencies Respond promptly to safety hazards, mitigate risks, and coordinate with designated staff members Ensure compliance with university policies and regulations, including parking enforcement, and refer infractions to the appropriate campus jurisdictional process Operate police and communication equipment, including assigned vehicles, to support law enforcement operations Direct and regulate crowds, traffic, parking, and pedestrian flow as needed to maintain safety and efficiency Prepare reports, conduct investigations, testify in court, and attend hearings as needed Ensure campus facilities are safe, secure, and properly maintained by conducting routine patrols, taking appropriate corrective actions, and reporting issues to designated staff for follow-up Foster positive interactions with students, staff, faculty, and visitors while conducting patrols and presenting educational outreach programs as assigned Requirements: Applicants must meet all requirements to be law enforcement officers in the Commonwealth of Virginia, as listed in Virginia Code 15.2-1705, as well as Longwood University's specific requirements, to include: High school diploma or equivalent Possess a valid Virginia driver's license, or the ability to obtain one, with a satisfactory driving record Selected candidates must be U.S. Citizens Upon successful completion of field training, selected candidates must fulfill a two-year contractual service commitment Proven ability to communicate and work effectively with a diverse population of students, faculty, staff, and visitors Satisfactory results on a pre-employment alcohol and drug test are required Successfully pass all required medical, drug, and psychological evaluations Successfully pass an extensive background investigation, including a fingerprint-based criminal background investigation Must be at least 21 years of age at the time of hire Must be available to work rotating shifts, including nights, weekends, and holidays Must serve a twelve-month probationary period Must successfully qualify for the use of department-issued weapons Directly related experience in high-stress environments, such as military, fire, or rescue services, is preferred and will be considered in the selection process Current Virginia DCJS Law Enforcement Certification, advanced DCJS certifications, or instructor-level training is preferred Prior experience in higher education, law enforcement, or campus security is preferred Additional Information: This is a full-time, classified, non-exempt position in pay band 3. The anticipated salary range for this position is $45,000 - $49,000 annually. A successful fingerprint-based criminal background investigation is required. AmeriCorps, Peace Corps, and other national service alumni are encouraged to apply. If a DCJS-certified applicant is selected, the hiring date will be set once all selection processes are complete. If an uncertified applicant is selected, the applicant will likely be hired as soon as possible and will be required to attend the next available basic law enforcement course at the Central Virginia Criminal Justice Academy (CVCJA). The training academy will be held at the Central Virginia Criminal Justice Academy (CVCJA) in Lynchburg, VA, anticipated to start in July 2026. Police recruits must provide their own transportation for travel to and from the academy. Commonwealth of Virginia benefits accompany this position to include: State health and dental benefits & flexible spending accounts Paid leave (which may include sick leave, personal leave, annual leave, etc.), and 13 holidays Retirement savings plans (some with limited employer match available (VRS)) Life & Long-Term care insurance Employee Assistance Program Employee discounts for various services, including Verizon Educational benefits for most employees Cost-effective Fitness Center membership for employees In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), Longwood University will provide, if requested, reasonable accommodations to applicants in order to provide access to the application and/or interview process. You are not required to note the presence of a disability on your application. If, however, you require accommodations in the application and/or interview process, please contact the Office of Human Resources at 434-395-2074 or humres@longwood.edu . Per CFR: Title 34, the Title IX Coordinator's contact information can be located through this link http://www.longwood.edu/titleix/ . Application Instructions: Review of applications will begin immediately. Position will be posted a minimum of five business days, position posted 3/27/2026. To apply for this position, qualified applicants must complete the online application and attach a resume and cover letter, and any other documents you wish to include. Applicants who meet the minimum requirements will be emailed a detailed background package that must be completed and returned. If you have been affected by DHRM Policy 1.30 Layoff, and possess a valid Interagency Placement Screening Form (Yellow Card) or a Preferential Hiring Card (Blue Card), you must upload a copy of your card when you submit your application/resume. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Longwood University 201 High Street Farmville, VA 23909"
    },
    "https://longwood.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205358": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Accounting (F0082)",
      "description": "Longwood University\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Accounting (F0082) Longwood University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Accounting (F0082) Title Careers Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of Accounting (F0082) Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: College of Business and Economics Locations: Farmville, VA Posted: Sep 30, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Exempt Ref. No.: F0082 Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $120,000.00 - $128,000.00 Position ID: 205358 Share About Longwood University: A comprehensive university with a strong liberal arts foundation, Longwood has a distinctive mission to develop citizen leaders who are prepared to make positive contributions to the common good of society. Founded in 1839, Longwood is the third-oldest public university in Virginia. Longwood is part of the proud tradition of higher education in the Commonwealth of Virginia. Roughly one hour's drive from Charlottesville, Lynchburg, and Richmond, Longwood is located in the historic two-college community of Farmville.  Longwood currently has approximately 4,700 undergraduate and graduate students and 42,000 alumni. It maintains affiliations with the neighboring Robert Russa Moton Museum of civil rights history and the Longwood Center for Visual Arts, a nationally accredited university art museum. A member of the Big South Conference, Longwood competes at the NCAA Division I level. Job Description: The Department of Accounting, Finance, Economics, and Information Systems in the College of Business and Economics is seeking a full-time, tenure-track position in accounting at the rank of Assistant Professor (F0082) beginning in August 2027. The AACSB-accredited College of Business and Economics offers an undergraduate degree in Business Administration with concentrations in six disciplines, including Accounting, as well as a fully online MBA program. The ideal candidate will have a demonstrated emphasis in teaching and research related to accounting. The candidate will also have the ability to teach a variety of subjects at the undergraduate level (BSBA) and graduate level (MBA), in areas including Principles, Tax Accounting, Fraud, and Accounting Information Systems courses. The successful candidate should have sufficient technical experience to provide hands-on experiences and meaningful instruction to supplement traditional textbook/lecture material for students. Applicants will be expected to contribute to excellence in education through teaching and service to the college, university, and community. This position is located in Farmville, Virginia, and is required to work in person on Longwood University's campus. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications The successful candidate will possess a Ph.D. in Accounting or a related field, preferably from an AACSB-accredited institution. ABD candidates will be considered but should be on schedule to complete their degree by August 2027. Candidate must demonstrate the ability to maintain a program of research output sufficient to meet AACSB scholarly academic (SA) status requirements. Additionally, the candidate must demonstrate the ability to meet annual progress toward scholarly output and tenure-track publication goals consistent with guidance in Longwood University's Faculty Policies & Procedures Manual. Preferred Qualifications Professional experience is preferred, but not required. Candidates with a CPA are preferred. Prior college-level and online teaching experience preferred. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to high-quality instruction in a student-centered environment, interest in active and collaborative learning and the instructional use of technology, and enthusiasm for working in a multidisciplinary environment. A demonstrated ability and commitment to working with a diverse group of students, faculty, staff, and constituents in support of the university's mission is preferred. Additional Information: This position is a full-time, tenure-track, instructional faculty position. The anticipated salary range for this position will be $120,000 - $128,000 annually. A successful fingerprint-based criminal background investigation is required. AmeriCorps, Peace Corps, and other national service alumni are encouraged to apply. Commonwealth of Virginia benefits accompany this position to include: State health and dental benefits & flexible spending accounts Paid leave (which may include sick leave, personal leave, annual leave, etc.), and 13 holidays Retirement savings plans (some with limited employer match available (VRS)) Life & Long-Term care insurance Employee Assistance Program Employee discounts for various services, including Verizon Educational benefits for most employees Cost-effective Fitness Center membership for employees In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), Longwood University will provide, if requested, reasonable accommodations to applicants in order to provide access to the application and/or interview process. You are not required to note the presence of a disability on your application. If, however, you require accommodations in the application and/or interview process, please contact the Office of Human Resources at 434-395-2074 or humres@longwood.edu . Per CFR: Title 34, the Title IX Coordinator's contact information can be located through this link http://www.longwood.edu/titleix/ . A diversified workforce is an important part of our strategic plan.  EOE/AA Application Instructions: Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled; position posted 9/30/2026. To apply for this position, qualified applicants must complete the online information section and questions, and please attach (under Resume): Letter of interest summarizing qualifications for this position Current curriculum vitae Unofficial graduate transcript Statement of teaching interests and philosophy, including how the candidate serves diverse populations and perspectives in the classroom Teaching evaluation summaries (if available) Contact information for three active faculty members who are familiar with the candidate's teaching and research and can discuss the candidate's academic qualifications for this position Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Longwood University 201 High Street Farmville, VA 23909"
    },
    "https://longwood.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203728": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biology (F0041)",
      "description": "Longwood University\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Biology (F0041) Longwood University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Biology (F0041) Title Careers Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of Biology (F0041) Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Biological-Env Sciences Locations: Farmville, VA Posted: Aug 14, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Exempt Ref. No.: F0041 Position ID: 203728 Share About Longwood University: A comprehensive university with a strong liberal arts foundation, Longwood has a distinctive mission to develop citizen leaders who are prepared to make positive contributions to the common good of society. Founded in 1839, Longwood is the third-oldest public university in Virginia. Longwood is part of the proud tradition of higher education in the Commonwealth of Virginia. Roughly one hour's drive from Charlottesville, Lynchburg, and Richmond, Longwood is located in the historic two-college community of Farmville.  Longwood currently has approximately 4,600 undergraduate and graduate students and 41,000 alumni. It maintains affiliations with the neighboring Robert Russa Moton Museum of civil rights history and the Longwood Center for Visual Arts, a nationally accredited university art museum. A member of the Big South Conference, Longwood competes at the NCAA Division I level. Job Description: The Department of Biological and Environmental Sciences in the Cook-Cole College of Arts & Sciences invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position (F0041) at the Assistant Professor level to begin in August 2027. We seek a broadly trained biologist whose research interests will complement those of our faculty. Teaching responsibilities include human anatomy and physiology (non-cadaver), introductory biology, and upper-level courses in the candidate's area of expertise. The standard teaching load is 12 contact hours per semester. In addition to the primary responsibility of innovative undergraduate teaching, faculty are also expected to advise students in the major, develop a research program involving undergraduates, and participate in service at the department and University level. The successful candidate will be provided with start-up funding and dedicated research space. Additionally, access will be provided to modern instrumentation, including digital PCR, flow cytometry, nanopore sequencer, high-speed cameras, and a range of microscopes (SEM, fluorescent, and digital confocal), and small-animal facilities. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to utilize the Environmental Education Center at Lancer Park and the Baliles Center for Environmental Education at Hull Springs . Longwood's Office of Student Research provides funding to support student-faculty research and travel, and the Center for Faculty Enrichment provides professional development resources and training. The successful candidate will also have the opportunity to contribute courses to Longwood's Brock Experiences , study abroad programs, and the Cormier Honors College . This position is located in Farmville, Virginia, and is required to work in person on Longwood University's campus. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Minimum Requirement: Earned Ph.D. by time of appointment in August 2027. Required commitment to excellence and innovation in undergraduate teaching, potential to develop a successful research program in an undergraduate setting, and dedication to quality advising of students and supervision of undergraduate research. Candidates with demonstrated college teaching ability and commitment to service preferred. A demonstrated ability and commitment to working with a diverse group of students, faculty, staff, and constituents in support of the university mission is preferred. Additional Information: This position is a full-time, tenure-track, instructional faculty position. The anticipated salary range for this position will be $63,000 - $69,000 annually. A successful fingerprint-based criminal background investigation is required. AmeriCorps, Peace Corps, and other national service alumni are encouraged to apply. Commonwealth of Virginia benefits accompany this position to include: State health and dental benefits & flexible spending accounts Paid leave (which may include sick leave, personal leave, annual leave, etc.), and 13 holidays Retirement savings plans (some with limited employer match available (VRS)) Life & Long-Term care insurance Employee Assistance Program Employee discounts for various services, including Verizon. Educational benefits for most employees Cost-effective Fitness Center membership for employees In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), Longwood University will provide, if requested, reasonable accommodations to applicants in order to provide access to the application and/or interview process. You are not required to note the presence of a disability on your application. If, however, you require accommodations in the application and/or interview process, please contact the Office of Human Resources at 434-395-2074 or humres@longwood.edu . Per CFR: Title 34, the Title IX Coordinator's contact information can be located through this link http://www.longwood.edu/titleix/ . A diversified workforce is an important part of our strategic plan.  EOE/AA Application Instructions: Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled, position posted 8/14/2026. To apply for this position, qualified applicants must complete the online information section and questions, and please attach (under Resume): Letter of interest summarizing qualifications for this position Current curriculum vitae Unofficial graduate transcripts Statement of teaching philosophy, including how the applicant serves diverse populations and perspectives in the classroom Statement of research interests, including how undergraduates could be involved in the research Contact information for three professional references Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Longwood University 201 High Street Farmville, VA 23909"
    },
