    "https://longwood.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203603": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Social Work (F0158)",
      "description": "Longwood University\nJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Social Work (F0158) Longwood University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Professor of Social Work (F0158) Title Careers Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Professor of Social Work (F0158) Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Social Work & Communication Sciences and Disorders Locations: Farmville, VA Posted: Aug 12, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Exempt Ref. No.: F0158 Position ID: 203603 Share About Longwood University: A comprehensive university with a strong liberal arts foundation, Longwood has a distinctive mission to develop citizen leaders who are prepared to make positive contributions to the common good of society. Founded in 1839, Longwood is the third-oldest public university in Virginia. Longwood is part of the proud tradition of higher education in the Commonwealth of Virginia. Roughly one hour's drive from Charlottesville, Lynchburg, and Richmond, Longwood is located in the historic two-college community of Farmville.  Longwood currently has approximately 4,600 undergraduate and graduate students and 41,000 alumni. It maintains affiliations with the neighboring Robert Russa Moton Museum of civil rights history and the Longwood Center for Visual Arts, a nationally accredited university art museum. A member of the Big South Conference, Longwood competes at the NCAA Division I level. Job Description: Longwood University's Social Work undergraduate program is fully accredited by the Council on Social Work Education (CSWE) and prepares generalist, entry-level Social Work Practitioners. The Department of Social Work and Communication Sciences and Disorders in the College of Education, Health, and Human Services invites applications for a tenure track, full-time faculty position (F0158) at the rank of Assistant Professor of Social Work. This position requires the skills, knowledge, and abilities to teach undergraduate social work courses that focus on generalist social work practice. Candidates who could support the development and delivery of a future Master's Degree of Social Work (MSW) program are strongly preferred. This position is located in Farmville, Virginia, and is required to work in person on Longwood University's campus. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Master's degree in social work (MSW) from a CSWE-accredited program. PhD preferred, in-progress doctoral candidates considered. Teaching experience in a CSWE-accredited program and post-MSW social work practice experience is required. Applicants must show clear evidence of excellence in teaching and service, and the potential for meaningful scholarship in social work. Additional Information: This position is a full-time, tenure-track instructional faculty position. The anticipated salary range for this position will be $68,000 - $74,000 annually. A successful fingerprint-based criminal background investigation is required. AmeriCorps, Peace Corps, and other national service alumni are encouraged to apply. Commonwealth of Virginia benefits accompany this position to include: State health and dental benefits & flexible spending accounts Paid leave (which may include sick leave, personal leave, annual leave, etc.), and 13 holidays Retirement savings plans (some with limited employer match available (VRS)) Life & Long-Term care insurance Employee Assistance Program Employee discounts for various services, including Verizon. Educational benefits for most employees Cost-effective Fitness Center membership for employees In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), Longwood University will provide, if requested, reasonable accommodations to applicants in order to provide access to the application and/or interview process. You are not required to note the presence of a disability on your application. If, however, you require accommodations in the application and/or interview process, please contact the Office of Human Resources at 434-395-2074 or humres@longwood.edu . Per CFR: Title 34, the Title IX Coordinator's contact information can be located through this link http://www.longwood.edu/titleix/ . A diversified workforce is an important part of our strategic plan.  EOE/AA Application Instructions: Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Position posted 8/12/2026. To apply for this position, qualified applicants must complete the online information section and questions, and please attach (under Resume): Letter of interest summarizing qualifications for this position Current curriculum vitae Unofficial graduate transcript Names and contact details for three references who can discuss the candidate's academic qualifications for this position Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Longwood University 201 High Street Farmville, VA 23909"
    },
    "https://longwood.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=199577": {
      "title": "Part-time Clinical Educator in Nursing (M0010)",
      "description": "Longwood University\nJob Posting: Part-time Clinical Educator in Nursing (M0010) Longwood University \n\tJob Posting: Part-time Clinical Educator in Nursing (M0010) Title Careers Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Part-time Clinical Educator in Nursing (M0010) Category: Faculty Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Nursing Program Locations: Farmville, VA Posted: Apr 16, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Ref. No.: M0010 Position ID: 199577 Share About Longwood University: A comprehensive university with a strong liberal arts foundation, Longwood has a distinctive mission to develop citizen leaders who are prepared to make positive contributions to the common good of society. Founded in 1839, Longwood is the third-oldest public university in Virginia. Longwood is part of the proud tradition of higher education in the Commonwealth of Virginia. Roughly one hour's drive from Charlottesville, Lynchburg, and Richmond, Longwood is located in the historic two-college community of Farmville.  Longwood currently has approximately 4,600 undergraduate and graduate students and 41,000 alumni. It maintains affiliations with the neighboring Robert Russa Moton Museum of civil rights history and the Longwood Center for Visual Arts, a nationally accredited university art museum. A member of the Big South Conference, Longwood competes at the NCAA Division I level. Job Description: The Department of Nursing is seeking candidates for a Part-time Clinical Educator in Nursing (M0010) for the Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) program at Longwood University. The mission of Longwood's BSN program is to promote excellence in nursing education and clinical competency; to promote the development of citizen leaders in the nursing profession; to promote partnerships to enhance health care and health care education in the region; to be one component of the solution to the nursing shortage; and to improve the health of local communities. This position will start Fall 2026. The successful candidate will instruct and evaluate BSN students in classroom, lab, and clinical site placement settings. Responsibilities will also include establishing and maintaining relationships with clinical sites and clinical preceptors, and providing oversight of clinical preceptors. The successful candidate also will represent the Longwood BSN program within the university, the larger community, and the professional community. This position is located in Farmville, Virginia, and is required to work in person on Longwood University's campus. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: Master's degree in nursing Must be licensed as a Registered Nurse with privileges in Virginia or eligible for such licensure Strong background and clinically competent in adult medical surgical (\"med surg\") Experience in mental health/community health and/or obstetrics/pediatrics is acceptable Additional Information: This position is a part-time, exempt, non-tenure-track, instructional faculty position that will start Fall 2026. Commonwealth of Virginia benefits do not accompany this position. Salary will be commensurate with credentials and experience. A successful fingerprint-based criminal background investigation is required. AmeriCorps, Peace Corps, and other national service alumni are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), Longwood University will provide, if requested, reasonable accommodations to applicants in need of accommodations in order to provide access to the application and/or interview process. You are not required to note the presence of a disability on your application. If, however, you require accommodations in the application and/or interview process, please contact the Office of Human Resources at 434-395-2074 or humres@longwood.edu . Per CFR: Title 34, the Title IX Coordinator's contact information can be located through this link http://www.longwood.edu/titleix/ . A diversified workforce is an important part of our strategic plan.  EOE/AA Application Instructions: Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled; position posted 4/16/2026. To apply for this position, qualified applicants must complete the online information section and questions, and please attach (under Resume): Letter of interest Current curriculum vitae Graduate transcripts Names and contact information for three (3) professional references Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Longwood University 201 High Street Farmville, VA 23909"
    },
    "https://longwood.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205863": {
      "title": "Athletics Academic Advisor / Education Support Specialist II (T0005)",
      "description": "Longwood University\nJob Posting: Athletics Academic Advisor / Education Support Specialist II (T0005) Longwood University \n\tJob Posting: Athletics Academic Advisor / Education Support Specialist II (T0005) Title Careers Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Athletics Academic Advisor / Education Support Specialist II (T0005) Category: Wage Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Athletics - Academic Services Locations: Farmville, VA Posted: Oct 16, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Temporary Ref. No.: (T0005) Salary Type: Hourly Salary Range: $25.93 - $29.63 Position ID: 205863 Share About Longwood University: A comprehensive university with a strong liberal arts foundation, Longwood has a distinctive mission to develop citizen leaders who are prepared to make positive contributions to the common good of society. Founded in 1839, Longwood is the third-oldest public university in Virginia. Longwood is part of the proud tradition of higher education in the Commonwealth of Virginia. Roughly one hour's drive from Charlottesville, Lynchburg, and Richmond, Longwood is located in the historic two-college community of Farmville. Longwood currently has approximately 4,700 undergraduate and graduate students and 42,000 alumni. It maintains affiliations with the neighboring Robert Russa Moton Museum of civil rights history and the Longwood Center for Visual Arts, a nationally accredited university art museum. A member of the Big South Conference, Longwood competes at the NCAA Division I level. Job Description: Longwood University invites qualified applicants to apply for the position of Athletics Academic Advisor / Education Support Specialist II (T0005). The Academic Advisor supports the academic success, retention, and graduation of NCAA Division I student-athletes. This position works with the Director of Athletic Academic Services to provide academic advising, monitor academic progress, coordinate learning support services, and collaborate with coaches, faculty, and campus partners to promote student-athlete achievement while ensuring compliance with NCAA, conference, and institutional policies. This position is located in Farmville, Virginia, and is required to work in person on Longwood University's campus. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Essential Responsibilities and Duties: Academic Advising & Student Support Provide academic counseling and support to assigned student-athlete populations. Assist student-athletes with course selection, degree planning, registration, and academic goal setting. Monitor academic progress toward degree completion and NCAA eligibility requirements. Conduct regular meetings with student-athletes to review academic performance and address challenges. Refer student-athletes to appropriate campus resources, including tutoring, writing centers, counseling services, and career development programs. Academic Monitoring Track attendance, assignment completion, and academic performance through communication with faculty and student-athletes. Review midterm and semester grades to identify students requiring academic intervention. Develop and implement individualized academic success plans for at-risk student-athletes. Maintain accurate academic records and documentation. Academic Support Programming Coordinate study hall programs and academic support services. Assist with the recruitment, training, and supervision of tutors and academic mentors. Support transition programming for first-year and transfer student-athletes. Participate in student-athlete development initiatives focused on time management, study skills, and academic achievement. Collaboration & Communication Maintain effective working relationships with coaches, faculty, academic departments, and campus administrators. Communicate academic progress and concerns to coaches in accordance with institutional and NCAA guidelines. Participate in departmental meetings and student success initiatives. Represent the athletics academic services office at university and athletics events as needed. Compliance & Record Management Ensure adherence to NCAA, conference, and institutional academic policies and regulations. Assist with eligibility certification processes and academic reporting requirements. Maintain confidentiality of student records in compliance with FERPA regulations. Prepare reports and academic assessments as requested. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Demonstrated commitment to student development and academic success. Strong interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills. Ability to work with diverse populations. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite and student information systems. Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: Strong advising and relationship-building skills. Ability to motivate and support student-athletes. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Strong attention to detail and recordkeeping abilities. Ability to analyze academic performance data and recommend interventions. Commitment to student success, academic integrity, and NCAA compliance. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution is preferred. Master's degree in Higher Education, Counseling, Student Affairs, Education, or a related field is strongly preferred. Experience working with college students, student-athletes, academic support programs, advising, tutoring, mentoring, or student success initiatives. Familiarity with NCAA rules and eligibility requirements. Experience in intercollegiate athletics or higher education. Additional Information: This is a part-time, temporary wage, non-exempt position in pay band 3, limited to an average of 29 hours per week and 1,500 hours maximum per work year. The anticipated hourly range for this position will be $25.93 - $29.63. Commonwealth of Virginia benefits do not accompany this position. A successful fingerprint-based criminal background investigation is required. AmeriCorps, Peace Corps, and other national service alumni are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), Longwood University will provide, if requested, reasonable accommodations to applicants in order to provide access to the application and/or interview process. You are not required to note the presence of a disability on your application. If, however, you require accommodations in the application and/or interview process, please contact the Office of Human Resources at 434-395-2074 or humres@longwood.edu . Per CFR: Title 34, the Title IX Coordinator's contact information can be located through this link http://www.longwood.edu/titleix/ . A diversified workforce is an important part of our strategic plan. EOE/AA Application Instructions: Review of applications will begin immediately. Position will be posted a minimum of five business days, position posted 10/16/2026. To apply for this position, qualified applicants must complete the online application and attach a resume, cover letter, and/or other documents. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Longwood University 201 High Street Farmville, VA 23909"
    },
    "https://longwood.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205342": {
      "title": "Part-time Assistant Early Childhood Teacher / Education Support Assistant (T0037)",
      "description": "Longwood University\nJob Posting: Part-time Assistant Early Childhood Teacher / Education Support Assistant (T0037) Longwood University \n\tJob Posting: Part-time Assistant Early Childhood Teacher / Education Support Assistant (T0037) Title Careers Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Part-time Assistant Early Childhood Teacher / Education Support Assistant (T0037) Category: Wage Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Andy Taylor Center Locations: Farmville, VA Posted: Sep 30, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Temporary Ref. No.: T0037 Position ID: 205342 Share About Longwood University: A comprehensive university with a strong liberal arts foundation, Longwood has a distinctive mission to develop citizen leaders who are prepared to make positive contributions to the common good of society. Founded in 1839, Longwood is the third-oldest public university in Virginia. Longwood is part of the proud tradition of higher education in the Commonwealth of Virginia. Roughly one hour's drive from Charlottesville, Lynchburg, and Richmond, Longwood is located in the historic two-college community of Farmville.  Longwood currently has approximately 4,700 undergraduate and graduate students and 42,000 alumni. It maintains affiliations with the neighboring Robert Russa Moton Museum of civil rights history and the Longwood Center for Visual Arts, a nationally accredited university art museum. A member of the Big South Conference, Longwood competes at the NCAA Division I level. Job Description: Longwood University invites qualified applicants to apply for the position of Part-time Assistant Early Childhood Teacher / Education Support Assistant (T0037) at the Andy Taylor Center for Early Childhood Development. The Andy Taylor Center is part of the Early Childhood Development Initiative (ECDI) in the College of Education, Health and Human Services at Longwood University. The Part-time Assistant Early Childhood Teacher will provide support to the Lead Teacher in the classroom. The Part-time Assistant Teacher will be responsible for assisting with planning, guiding, and assessing instruction. The selected candidate will also be responsible for collaborating with Lead Teachers to ensure smooth transitions, similar expectations throughout the day, and efficient planning. Additionally, the Part-time Assistant Teacher will facilitate open communication with families. This position will report to the Site Director. This position is located in Farmville, Virginia, and is required to work in person on Longwood University's campus. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Requirements: The ECDI seeks candidates with experience working in project-based early childhood programming, preferably Reggio-inspired teaching. Candidates should have experience working in early childhood education, early childhood special education, or related fields. Early childhood credentials or Associate's degree preferred. Candidates should be able to demonstrate knowledge of the development of young children and knowledge of and/or training in emergent curriculum and documentation. It is also preferred that candidates have experience collaboratively teaching in a school or childcare center with children birth to age five. Must be able to perform physical activities associated with the care of infants and toddlers. Additional Information: This is a part-time, temporary wage, non-exempt position in pay band 1. The anticipated pay range for this position will be $14.11 - $17.00 per hour. Hours worked will vary based on need, but will be limited to an average of 29 hours per week and 1,500 hours maximum per work year. Commonwealth of Virginia benefits do not accompany this position. A successful fingerprint-based criminal background investigation is required. AmeriCorps, Peace Corps, and other national service alumni are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), Longwood University will provide, if requested, reasonable accommodations to applicants in order to provide access to the application and/or interview process. You are not required to note the presence of a disability on your application. If, however, you require accommodations in the application and/or interview process, please contact the Office of Human Resources at 434-395-2074 or humres@longwood.edu . Per CFR: Title 34, the Title IX Coordinator's contact information can be located through this link http://www.longwood.edu/titleix/ . A diversified workforce is an important part of our strategic plan.  EOE/AA Application Instructions: Review of applications will begin immediately. Position will be posted a minimum of five business days, position posted 9/30/2026. To apply for this position, qualified applicants must complete the online application and attach a resume, cover letter, and any other documents you wish to include with your application materials. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Longwood University 201 High Street Farmville, VA 23909"
    },
