    "https://longwood.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203401": {
      "title": "Part-Time Plumbing Steamfitter / Utility Plant Specialist II (T0189)",
      "description": "Longwood University\nJob Posting: Part-Time Plumbing Steamfitter / Utility Plant Specialist II (T0189) Longwood University \n\tJob Posting: Part-Time Plumbing Steamfitter / Utility Plant Specialist II (T0189) Title Careers Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Part-Time Plumbing Steamfitter / Utility Plant Specialist II (T0189) Category: Wage Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Facilities Management and Operations Locations: Farmville, VA Posted: Aug 5, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Non-Exempt Ref. No.: (T0189) Position ID: 203401 Share About Longwood University: A comprehensive university with a strong liberal arts foundation, Longwood has a distinctive mission to develop citizen leaders who are prepared to make positive contributions to the common good of society. Founded in 1839, Longwood is the third-oldest public university in Virginia. Longwood is part of the proud tradition of higher education in the Commonwealth of Virginia. Roughly one hour's drive from Charlottesville, Lynchburg, and Richmond, Longwood is located in the historic two-college community of Farmville.  Longwood currently has approximately 4,600 undergraduate and graduate students and more than 41,000 alumni. It maintains affiliations with the neighboring Robert Russa Moton Museum of civil rights history and the Longwood Center for Visual Arts, a nationally accredited university art museum. A member of the Big South Conference, Longwood competes at the NCAA Division I level. Job Description: Longwood University invites qualified applicants to apply for the part-time position of Plumbing Steamfitter / Utility Plant Specialist II (T0189). The successful candidate will be responsible for the shift operation of the 101,400 lb./hour heating plant and distribution system to ensure the plant is operated safely, efficiently, and in compliance with all environmental rules and regulations. This position is considered emergency personnel, which requires the selected candidate to report to work or be called in due to inclement weather, an emergency, staff shortage, etc. This position is located in Farmville, Virginia, and is required to work in person on Longwood University's campus. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Essential Responsibilities and Duties: Perform routine equipment operating tasks; start-up and secure equipment promptly, and properly respond to changing load demand and fuel quality conditions Assist with outages for maintenance and repairs of plant equipment Determine required equipment and welding methods, applying knowledge of metallurgy, geometry, and welding techniques Ability to follow industry standard practices and/or specific guidelines, particularly as they relate to safety, health, and environmental practices Ability to work on elevated structures and in confined spaces Notify and coordinate steam outages for the maintenance and repair of equipment and/or piping within the university Maintain the cleanliness of utility tunnels, manholes, mechanical rooms, and work areas. Perform welding and maintenance duties within the Heating Plant Inspect all high-pressure, medium-pressure, and low-pressure steam systems and components for the purpose of ensuring safety, performing necessary repairs, and providing an ongoing program of preventative maintenance Proficiently monitor steam and condensate controls using electronic and manual equipment Perform welding and/or repairs on high-pressure and low-pressure steam, water, oil, and air piping; reseating and repairing valves; replacing gaskets; dismantling, repairing, and assembling equipment; the removal and replacement of parts; and assisting in the repair of general steam plant and campus-wide steam-related equipment Respond to steam-related emergency situations during normal business hours or after hours for the purpose of resolving immediate safety concerns Responsible for dumping ash trailers and wood debris trailers Responsible for minor maintenance of the welding truck and inventory of welding-related tools and supplies Other duties as assigned Requirements: High school diploma or equivalent required Valid driver's license required Basic computer knowledge Working knowledge of the design and function of utility-related equipment Advanced knowledge and skill in the operation and maintenance/repair of mechanical, electrical, pneumatic, and hydraulic equipment Advanced knowledge in monitoring, recording, sampling, and testing utilities while performing high safety practices Effective interpersonal and communication skills Must be able, if necessary, to work extended or irregular hours 6G welding certification preferred Confined space certification preferred Additional Information: This is a part-time, non-exempt, temporary wage position in pay band 3. The anticipated pay range for this position is $17.00 - $25.00 per hour. Hours worked will vary based on need, but will be limited to an average of 29 hours per week and 1,500 hours maximum per work year. Commonwealth of Virginia benefits do not accompany this position. A successful fingerprint-based criminal background investigation is required. AmeriCorps, Peace Corps, and other national service alumni are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), Longwood University will provide, if requested, reasonable accommodations to applicants in order to provide access to the application and/or interview process. You are not required to note the presence of a disability on your application. If, however, you require accommodations in the application and/or interview process, please contact the Office of Human Resources at 434-395-2074 or humres@longwood.edu . Per CFR: Title 34, the Title IX Coordinator's contact information can be located through this link http://www.longwood.edu/titleix/ . A diversified workforce is an important part of our strategic plan. EOE/AA Application Instructions: Review of applications will begin immediately. Position will be posted a minimum of five business days, position posted 8/5/2026. To apply for this position, qualified applicants must complete the online application and attach a resume, cover letter, and any other documents you wish to include with your application materials. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Longwood University 201 High Street Farmville, VA 23909"
